        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Memory-Enforced GPU Sharing in Kubernetes with NVIDIA CUDA 13.4 | NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Memory-Enforced GPU Sharing in Kubernetes with NVIDIA CUDA 13.4",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "It runs alongside the NVIDIA GPU Operator to set up and supervise Multi-Process Service (MPS) on every GPU node, apply per-workload memory limits and compute modes, and measure memory and compute use per GPU fraction rather than per whole GPU.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "CUDA 13.4 introduces a memory boundary enforcement that is transparent to applications, offering exact memory amounts, guaranteed minimums with burstable maximums, and a choice between time-slicing and sm-sharing compute modes.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "KAI Scheduler v0.18.0 integrates with GPU Fractioning through its NvFractions GPU-sharing mode, writing per-container Pod annotations that specify memory requests, limits, compute mode, and GPU device assignments for the operator to enforce on the node.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "CUDA 13.4 now enforces a memory boundary that is transparent to the application with a new time-sharing mode, alongside the compute sharing mode (sm-sharing) that already existed in MPS.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Table 1: Per-container Pod annotations that GPU Fractioning Operator reads to enforce a GPU fraction",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Any Kubernetes scheduler that can write these annotations can enforce GPU fractions with CUDA.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "KAI Scheduler picks which slice of which GPU each workload gets and writes the annotations (see Table 1, above), and gpu-fractioning enforces them on the node.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Call n the number of workloads sharing a GPU: either way each gets roughly 1/n of the compute, and what differs is whether they take turns or run together.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://developer.nvidia.com/blog/memory-enforced-gpu-sharing-in-kubernetes-with-nvidia-cuda-13-4/",
        "source": "NVIDIA Technical Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-27T20:50:39.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:27.384Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
